From 0018-cs4208-split-speakers Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Chicherin <ashzak990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 0018/0018] ALSA: hda/cs420x: optional separate PCM for the second MacBookPro11,x speaker pair

The MacBookPro11,x drives two stereo speaker pairs from two stereo DACs of
the CS4208: DAC 0x03 -> pin 0x12 ("Speaker") and DAC 0x04 -> pin 0x13
("Bass Speaker").  The generic parser exposes them as a 4-channel PCM, but
that PCM is completely silent, on all four drivers.

Measured on a MacBookPro11,3 with hda-verb while a stream was playing:

* a DAC outputs nothing while its converter format says 3 or 4 channels
  (0x12/0x13); rewriting it to the 2-channel format (0x11) makes it play;
* with the 2-channel format it plays only from channel offset 0; offsets 1
  and 2 are silent, the stripe control changes nothing;
* GPIO1 and the vendor coefficients (0x00-0x40) are identical between the
  playing and the silent state;
* two streams at once work: DAC 0x04 pointed at a second stream tag plays
  that stream while DAC 0x03 keeps playing the first.

So one multi-channel stream cannot feed the two pairs different signals, and
a tweeter/woofer crossover needs one stream per pair.  Add the module
parameter split_speakers (default off).  When set, the MBP11 fixup takes the
second speaker DAC out of the multi-out set and hands it to the generic
parser's alternate playback PCM ("CS4208 Alt Analog", device 2); the main
PCM becomes plain stereo on the first pair.

Without the parameter nothing changes: a stereo stream is still copied to
both pairs.

Signed-off-by: Igor Chicherin <ashzak990@gmail.com>
---
 sound/hda/codecs/cirrus/cs420x.c |   42 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 41 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/sound/hda/codecs/cirrus/cs420x.c
+++ b/sound/hda/codecs/cirrus/cs420x.c
@@ -17,6 +17,22 @@
 #include "hda_jack.h"
 #include "../generic.h"
 
+/*
+ * MacBookPro11,x have two stereo speaker pairs on two stereo DACs (0x03 -> pin
+ * 0x12 "Speaker", 0x04 -> pin 0x13 "Bass Speaker").  The CS4208 analog DACs
+ * only play a stream whose converter format says 2 channels, and only from
+ * channel offset 0: the 4-channel "surround" PCM is silent on all four drivers,
+ * and a 2-channel format at channel offset 2 is silent too.  Two separate
+ * streams do work.  With split_speakers=1 the second pair gets its own PCM
+ * ("Alt Analog", device 2) instead of a copy of the front channels, so
+ * userspace can run a tweeter/woofer crossover.  Off by default: a plain
+ * stereo stream then reaches only the first pair.
+ */
+static bool split_speakers;
+module_param(split_speakers, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(split_speakers,
+		 "CS4208 MacBookPro11,x: second speaker pair on its own PCM device (default=0)");
+
 struct cs_spec {
 	struct hda_gen_spec gen;
 
@@ -667,6 +683,30 @@
 	}
 }
 
+/* MacBookPro11,x: S/PDIF switch hook, plus the optional speaker split */
+static void cs4208_fixup_mbp11(struct hda_codec *codec,
+			       const struct hda_fixup *fix, int action)
+{
+	struct cs_spec *spec = codec->spec;
+	struct hda_gen_spec *gen = &spec->gen;
+
+	cs4208_fixup_spdif_switch(codec, fix, action);
+
+	/* after the pin parser has assigned the DACs, before the PCMs are built */
+	if (action != HDA_FIXUP_ACT_PROBE || !split_speakers)
+		return;
+	if (gen->autocfg.line_out_type != AUTO_PIN_SPEAKER_OUT ||
+	    gen->multiout.num_dacs != 2 || gen->alt_dac_nid) {
+		codec_warn(codec, "split_speakers: unexpected speaker layout, not splitting\n");
+		return;
+	}
+	gen->alt_dac_nid = gen->multiout.dac_nids[1];
+	gen->multiout.num_dacs = 1;
+	gen->multiout.max_channels = 2;
+	codec_info(codec, "split_speakers: DAC 0x%02x on the Alt Analog PCM\n",
+		   gen->alt_dac_nid);
+}
+
 static const struct hda_fixup cs4208_fixups[] = {
 	[CS4208_MBA6] = {
 		.type = HDA_FIXUP_PINS,
@@ -676,7 +716,7 @@
 	},
 	[CS4208_MBP11] = {
 		.type = HDA_FIXUP_FUNC,
-		.v.func = cs4208_fixup_spdif_switch,
+		.v.func = cs4208_fixup_mbp11,
 		.chained = true,
 		.chain_id = CS4208_GPIO0,
 	},
